  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoadingManager
  loadingCanvasGroup: {fileID: 2769491666205598954}
  loadingText: {fileID: 3042988947818961160}
  hintText: {fileID: 7796179387636028046}
  blackFadeGroup: {fileID: 7697764664862864318}
  loadingSpinner: {fileID: 4324903721984962745}
  loadingArt: {fileID: 5557195391690374394}
  loadingSprites:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: c06ffdf3908c4ec4c8712d49a7985b2c, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5245436c0a64fb44389f33f0a96d6576, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1d1ab76c736922e4ab0c9ee5ffb21248, type: 3}
  sceneFadeSpeed: 1.5
  hintChangeInterval: 10
  spinnerRotationSpeed: 150
  gameHints:
  - The Kingdom of Aethelgard does not forgive mistakes. Always compare your Power
    with the Recommended Power of a region before venturing out.
  - Retreat is not cowardice. If a battle turns against you, it is better to Give
    Up and return to Camp than to perish in the woods.
  - Grenades are your best friend against a crowd. Use them to thin the enemy ranks
    before drawing your sword.
  - Even the thickest helmet won't save you if you stand still. Keep moving during
    combat.
  - Conquered territories provide passive income. Don't forget to regularly collect
    resources from your domain.
  - Invest wood, stone, and food to upgrade your controlled regions. Higher levels
    yield more resources per hour.
  - Gems are incredibly rare. Spend them wisely and save them for the most crucial
    upgrades.
  - A well-fed warrior fights better. A steady supply of food from your territories
    is vital for expanding your influence.
  - Explore the World Map thoroughly. New territories can hide both vast riches and
    lethal dangers.
  - They say in Stonefall Quarry, undead miners still mindlessly swing their pickaxes.
    Stay on your guard.
  - Your Camp is the only truly safe haven in all of Aethelgard. Return there to
    catch your breath by the fire.
  - The dead do not feel pain, but they can still be hacked to pieces. Keep your
    blade sharp.
  - Only the strongest and most ruthless rulers can unite the fractured Kingdom of
    Aethelgard. Will you be one of them?
  - The dense, dark forests and steep cliffs of Aethelgard show no mercy to those
    who lose their focus.
  - "New armor doesn't just increase your defense\u2014it changes your appearance.
    Find gear worthy of a true lord."
  - Always check the Notice Board in your Camp. It frequently offers new, lucrative
    contracts and missions.
  - Heavy armor provides excellent protection against direct hits, but it slows you
    down. Find your perfect balance in battle.
  - Getting dizzy from the action? You can always disable Screen Shake or adjust
    your Mouse Sensitivity in the Settings menu.
